-
link(rel="stylesheet" href="static/asset/css/customcharts.css")
div
  .card
    .card-header
      p.card-header-title
        span.icon
          i.mdi.mdi-book-open-variant
        | How to Play Custom Charts
    .card-content
      .content
        h4 Prerequisites
        ol
          li
            | Download #[strong ifs_layeredfs] (#[code ifs_hook.dll]) from
            |  #[a(href="https://github.com/mon/ifs_layeredfs/releases" target="_blank") GitHub releases].
            | This is a DLL hook that allows the game to load custom content from the #[code data_mods] folder.
          li Place #[code ifs_hook.dll] in the same folder as #[code spice64.exe].
          li
            | Open #[strong spicecfg.exe], go to #[strong Options] → #[strong Inject DLL Hooks],
            |  and add #[code ifs_hook.dll] to the list.

        hr

        h4 Setup Custom Charts Sync
        ol
          li
            | Download the sync bundle below and extract both files next to #[code spice64.exe]:
          .field(style="margin-top:1.5rem;margin-bottom:1rem")
            a.button.is-success(href="/api/nautica/sync-bundle")
              span.icon
                i.mdi.mdi-download
              span Download Sync Bundle (.zip)
          li The bundle contains:
            ul(style="margin-bottom:1.5rem")
              li #[code sync_custom_charts.ps1] — the sync script that downloads charts from the server
              li #[code sync_and_play.bat] — a launcher that runs the sync script then starts the game
          li
            | Your folder should now look like this:
            pre(style="background:#1a1a1e;color:#ddd;padding:1em;border-radius:6px;font-size:0.85em;margin-top:0.5rem")
              | your_game_folder/
              |   spice64.exe
              |   spicecfg.exe
              |   ifs_hook.dll
              |   sync_custom_charts.ps1
              |   sync_and_play.bat
              |   data_mods/          ← created automatically on first sync

        hr

        h4 Playing
        ol
          li Run #[strong sync_and_play.bat] instead of launching the game directly.
          li The script will check for new custom charts on the server and download them automatically.
          li After syncing, the game launches normally. Custom charts appear in the song list.
          li On subsequent launches, the script only downloads if new charts are available — otherwise it starts instantly.



        div(style="margin-top:2rem")
          a.button.is-link(href="/plugin/sdvx@asphyxia/custom%20charts")
            span.icon
              i.mdi.mdi-arrow-left
            span Back to Custom Charts
